The native tray is MIT-licensed, not AGPL like the daemon it talks to. It is a
client: it speaks to sukarfleetd over the daemon's local HTTP API and ships as a
separate binary, so embedding it or building on it carries no copyleft duty.

Full text: ../../LICENSES/MIT.txt
Rationale and the licence boundary for the whole repository: ../../LICENSING.md

Two things in this directory are outside that MIT grant.

src/fonts/*.woff2 is a different licence entirely: it covers the bundled IBM
Plex Sans font files, which are not ours. IBM's copyright notice and the
Reserved Font Name are in src/fonts/LICENSE.txt; the SIL Open Font License 1.1
itself is in ../../LICENSES/OFL-1.1.txt, and OFL condition 2 means both have to
travel with any copy of those files.

brand/ holds the project's marks -- the sukarfleet symbol and wordmark -- along
with every icon derived from them under src-tauri/icons/ and src/assets/. Those
are not licensed under MIT and are excluded from the grant: MIT covers the code,
not the identity. Use them to refer to sukarfleet, not to imply the project
endorses you and not to brand other software.
